{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 2360566,
  "courseSlug": "sveltejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Svelte.js - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689658",
      "title": "Relying on Automatic Number Conversion",
      "lectureOrder": 84,
      "videoOrder": 74,
      "sourceHash": "fd76d113739a08f0240b5535f364306d40239ca58c681853b9bdf89207ee26cf",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2,
          "end": 6.44,
          "en": "Now let's go back to inputs, therefore, because they are such an important use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.89,
          "end": 13.37,
          "en": "Let me add another input here in the app component and let's set the type here to number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 13.61,
          "end": 19.46,
          "en": "Number is a valid input type, which for example gives us special controls that make it easier to enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 19.46,
          "end": 20.12,
          "en": "a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.95,
          "end": 22.46,
          "en": "Here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.46,
          "end": 24.5,
          "en": "Let's say we store that as a price.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.5,
          "end": 25.76,
          "en": "Initially, it's zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.76,
          "end": 34.88,
          "en": "And let me start with the longer form I bind price and here on input I get an event and for now I will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.88,
          "end": 41.12,
          "en": "actually simply console log the event target value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 42.97,
          "end": 44.14,
          "en": "And I'll soon change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 44.14,
          "end": 45.49,
          "en": "So this is not two way binding here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.49,
          "end": 47.47,
          "en": "I'm just logging whatever the user enters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.59,
          "end": 48.85,
          "en": "So here we have the price.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.85,
          "end": 51.04,
          "en": "Here you see the special number controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.04,
          "end": 55.42,
          "en": "And as I choose one here, you see, I'm logging that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.01,
          "end": 56.79,
          "en": "In here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.82,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "Now, please note that this number one, two, three, four.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 62.03,
          "en": "These numbers are black.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "Whereas the one here from my toggle is blue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 72.18,
          "en": "It might not look like much, but the difference actually is that this is a number regarding its data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "type, whereas this is treated as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.88,
          "end": 83.26,
          "en": "This can lead to strange bugs where you start adding two numbers together and you don't convert them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 83.26,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "to numbers before doing so, and then you would simply concatenate two strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 88.18,
          "end": 94.47999999999999,
          "en": "So let's say, for example, here I would have another number which actually is a string fetched from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 94.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.47999999999999,
          "en": "another input, and I add event target value and then I output the result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 101.05,
          "end": 107.74000000000001,
          "en": "Now when I enter one here, the result is not two but 11 because it's a concatenated string, one plus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 107.74000000000001,
          "end": 109.81,
          "en": "one concatenated as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 109.84,
          "end": 113.56,
          "en": "This is the default behavior of inputs in the Dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 113.56,
          "end": 117.1,
          "en": "In JavaScript you get the value as a string, always as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 117.1,
          "end": 121.12,
          "en": "Even if the type is number, the type does not affect the data type you're getting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 121.12,
          "end": 125.8,
          "en": "It instead affects how this input is presented and which controls you're seeing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 126.37,
          "end": 129.31,
          "en": "However, svelte helps you here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 129.31,
          "end": 136.63,
          "en": "If you're using the two way binding syntax with the Bind directive and you bind the value here to price",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 136.75,
          "end": 139.3,
          "en": "and I output my price here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 142.51,
          "end": 143.62,
          "en": "You will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 144.45,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "That's.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "Well, that actually converts this for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.97,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "You got undefined when it was empty because this is not a valid number and you got a warning that undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 152.67000000000002,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "is not a valid number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "So Svelte is checking this for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 155.25,
          "end": 157.59,
          "en": "And then you see this one here is blue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 157.59,
          "end": 161.67000000000002,
          "en": "And the reason for that being blue is indeed that it is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 161.67000000000002,
          "end": 168.51,
          "en": "So now when you're fetching data from inputs with type number or also with type range, you automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "get numbers and you don't manually need to convert this before using it in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
